{title: The Plot of Jezreel}
{subtitle: 2 Kings 9:1–37}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Elisha called a son of prophets
Take the flask and go to Ra-moth-gi-lead
Find Jehu son of Jehoshaphat
Pour the [Bb]oil on his [Dm]head
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
This is what the Lord says
I anoint you king over Israel
Strike down the house of Ahab
Avenge [Bb]the blood of prophets
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Je[Dm]hu rode to Jezreel city
Joram asked if it came in peace
He drew his bow and shot the king
Between the shoul[Bb]ders and the heart
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm]Throw him on the plot of Naboth
Repent for the blood of the prophet
Ahaziah fled to Megiddo
Where he died in [Bb]his chariot
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Je[Dm]zebel looked out the window
Asking if Zimri came in peace
He called for help and they threw her down
Trampled by the [Bb]horses
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
They found [Dm]only skull and feet
No one could bury her body
Dogs devoured her in Jezreel
As Elijah had foretold
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
This [Bb]is the word of [Dm]the Lord
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
